# Stable name for the Tonex ONE, and keep ModemManager away from it.
#
# ModemManager probes any CDC-ACM device and sends AT commands at it. On a
# pedal that answers a binary protocol, that is the classic footgun: the
# handshake appears to work intermittently and nothing explains why. Rule it
# out here rather than debugging it later.
# TAG+="systemd" is what makes a dev-tonex.device unit exist. Without it the
# service's `After=dev-tonex.device` orders against a unit systemd never
# creates, so the ordering silently does nothing.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1963", ATTRS{idProduct}=="00d1", \
  SYMLINK+="tonex", MODE="0660", GROUP="dialout", \
  ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}="1", TAG+="systemd"
